read-only-before-authorization: reject commands not permitted in Read-Only mode before authorization

Classification: spec-deviation bug fix.

Specification (TPM 2.0 Part 1, "Read-Only Mode of Operation", "Description"):
"A device supporting Read-Only mode must reject any affected command before
performing authorization checks which would be evaluated during the execution
of the command." Part 3, TPM2_ReadOnlyControl, Table "Commands Permitted in
Read-Only Mode": TPM2_NV_Write, TPM2_NV_Extend, TPM2_NV_SetBits,
TPM2_NV_WriteLock and TPM2_NV_ReadLock are "Permitted only when the NV index is
defined with TPMA_NV_ORDERLY and TPMA_NV_CLEAR_STCLEAR"; TPM2_PolicySecret is
"Not permitted when used with a PIN Pass/Fail NV index".

The reference rejects the commands that are never permitted (RO_DISALLOW)
right after the command code, but checks the entity-dependent ones in the
command actions (NvReadOnlyModeChecks(), TPM2_PolicySecret()), i.e. after the
authorization area has been processed: a failed authorization is reported
instead of TPM_RC_READ_ONLY and, for a PIN index authorizing
TPM2_PolicySecret, increments its pinCount (an NV write in Read-Only mode), or
the DA failure counter. The checks now also run in ExecuteCommand() once the
handles are validated (EntityGetLoadStatus()) and before the authorization
area, as in tpm-rs (TpmEngine::check_read_only_entities).
diff --git a/TPMCmd/tpm/src/main/ExecCommand.c b/TPMCmd/tpm/src/main/ExecCommand.c
--- a/TPMCmd/tpm/src/main/ExecCommand.c
+++ b/TPMCmd/tpm/src/main/ExecCommand.c
@@ -192,6 +192,37 @@ LIB_EXPORT void ExecuteCommand(
     result = EntityGetLoadStatus(&command);
     if(result != TPM_RC_SUCCESS)
         goto Cleanup;
+#if CC_ReadOnlyControl
+    // tpm-rs differential testing -- spec deviation fix (NOT determinism): Part 1,
+    // "Read-Only Mode of Operation": "A device supporting Read-Only mode must reject
+    // any affected command before performing authorization checks which would be
+    // evaluated during the execution of the command." Upstream checks the commands
+    // that are permitted only on some entities (Part 3, TPM2_ReadOnlyControl) in
+    // their actions, i.e. after the authorization (whose failure updates the DA
+    // counter or a PIN index's pinCount); check them before the authorization area.
+    if(gc.readOnly)
+    {
+        switch(command.code)
+        {
+            case TPM_CC_NV_Write:
+            case TPM_CC_NV_Extend:
+            case TPM_CC_NV_SetBits:
+            case TPM_CC_NV_WriteLock:
+            case TPM_CC_NV_ReadLock:
+                result = NvReadOnlyModeChecks(
+                    NvGetIndexInfo(command.handles[1], NULL)->publicArea.attributes);
+                break;
+            case TPM_CC_PolicySecret:
+                if(NvIsPinCountedIndex(command.handles[0]))
+                    result = TPM_RC_READ_ONLY;
+                break;
+            default:
+                break;
+        }
+        if(result != TPM_RC_SUCCESS)
+            goto Cleanup;
+    }
+#endif
     // Authorization session handling for the command.
     ClearCpRpHashes(&command);
     if(command.tag == TPM_ST_SESSIONS)
